    <DataNode elementId="AT1G67990-MONOMER" textLabel="Tapetum-specific methyltransferase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9C9W4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="335" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">At1G67990 was expressed in E. coli, purified and analyzed for enzyme activity |CITS: [19077165]|. The recombinant enzyme was found to catalyze the methylation of caffeoyl-CoA, trihydroxyferuloyl spermidine and tricaffeoyl spermidine. Mono- and di-methylated intermediates were identified, in addition to the tri-methylated products. It is noteworthy that although in vitro enzyme assays detected At1G67990 activity with tricaffeoyl spermidine, there may be other unknown methyltransferases involved in the O-methylation of tricaffeoyl spermidine in vivo. This was indicated in At1G67990 RNAi silenced mutants, where trihydroxyferuloyl spermidine was increasingly accumulated, but no accumulation of tricaffeoyl spermidine was found |CITS: [19077165]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G67990-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G67990.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR10509" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9C9W4" />
